From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:14:26 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 95/96] Plutonium: a parked window stays invisible when Ash
 demotes it

A parked window is hidden by its layer's opacity alone, and floats above
normal windows (for its popups). When a window goes fullscreen on its
display, as a shell's window does when the shell is turned on again,
WorkspaceLayoutManager::UpdateAlwaysOnTop() demotes floating windows with
WindowState::DisableZOrdering(), which hides and shows each one. The show
animation ends at opacity 1, so every parked window there was drawn as
itself above the shells: square, at its element's last place, taking no
input, and left there when its element moved or went away. Parked windows,
and hidden popups (hidden the same way), have kAnimationsDisabledKey until
they are shown again.

WaylandDmabufFeedbackManager::MaybeResendFeedback() cleared a scanout
candidate's scanout tranche on a display change without checking it had
one; a display with no scanout formats gives none (a window first shown
on the second display of an X11-hosted session DCHECKed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
